            <ArticleTitle>Absent septal q wave: the neglected deflection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-22, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Absence of the normal septal q wave in leads I and V6 is often overlooked. It correlates with a range of pathologic changes, including septal scarring and incomplete left bundle branch block.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
